-## Release train
-
-> Retired 2026-11-07: releases are cut per change by semantic version (AGENTS.md "Versioning is semantic"), not on a calendar.
-
-A release is a cut, not a goal (user, 2026-11-06: "make sure to hit the marks
-so we don't spend ages between stable test releases"). Two trains a week on
-fixed dates; the scope is what is green at the cut. Each train carries at most
-three MUSTS; a must that is not green 4 h before the cut slips to the next
-train, never the date. The last 4 h are the freeze: no new agents, the full
-gate (every crate, ui from crates/ui, clippy, all heavy lanes), bump, lock
-sync, tag, zip - the 0.7.0 recipe in RECOMMENDED "Release 0.7.0". Every cut is
-published by the session: the cut pushes main, then the tag, which fires
-release.yml (AGENTS.md "Every cut tag is published", user 2026-11-07).
-
-| Train | Cut (local) | Theme | Musts | Nice-to-have |
-|---|---|---|---|---|
-| **0.8.0** | CUT Fri 2026-11-06 (early, to park) - tag v0.8.0 on b78b25b, dist/camcraft-0.8.0-win-x64.zip; carries most of 0.9.0 and 0.10.0 too (RECOMMENDED "Release 0.8.0") | Every 0.7.0 known limit closed; the zip runs on any machine | themes resolved beside the exe (M13.3); M11.3 ✅; M13.7 ✅ (mid-move pose decided) | M11.4 island on HSM + slot entry kinks; M13.8 ✅; material.rs split; `scripts/release.ps1` (one command: gate → bump → zip) |
